t(id="MC-4", slug="mcp-wire-projection", title="Slim the MCP wire by projecting duplicated envelope fields away",
  s=["S-26"], wave=3, area=["mcp"], tier="Sonnet", size="S",
  why="57-58% of a standards `semantic_search` response is envelope rather than passage (k=10 is about 4.2k tokens; a Waymo call averages about 10.8k): `bbox`, a `snippet` that lies inside `passage_text` for 94-100% of results, and repeated `paper_id`/`block_id`. Agents already lower `k` to cope (RV-4 F-4.6; review S-26).",
  in_=["In `app/serve.py`, project the response with `model_dump(exclude=...)` for `bbox`, the duplicated `anchor.snippet` and the repeated `anchor.paper_id`/`citation.paper_id`; the contract objects are untouched.","Starts only if the operator answers F5 yes (the wire may be a projection of the frozen envelope)."],
  out=["Snippet-only passages by default (the logs show search-then-`get_span` verification habits). Changing `search_papers` section paths (`PaperSummaryView`, a contract change). `get_span` behaviour."],
  owns=["app/serve.py","app/test_serve.py","scripts/mcp_wire_tokens.py","scripts/test_mcp_wire_tokens.py"],
  commits=["stub: docstring stating the projection list and the invariant that `passage_text`, `citation` and `get_span(anchor)` round-trip are unchanged","failing tests: projected JSON lacks the four fields; `passage_text` and `citation` equal the unprojected values; `get_span` on a projected anchor still resolves","implementation to green","token-count script (skips cleanly if the tokenizer package is absent) and measurement on standards- and Waymo-sized fixtures"],
  verify=["`conda run -n agent-rag-research python -m pytest -q app/test_serve.py scripts/test_mcp_wire_tokens.py -o addopts=\"--disable-socket\"`","Token count before/after on a realistic response fixture quoted in the PR"],
  accept="Token count of a standards k=10 response falls by at least 25% with identical `passage_text` and citation content; `get_span` still round-trips. Falsified if `passage_text` differs anywhere or the drop is under 25%.",
  deps=["MC-3"], ext=["F5"], gates=["EP-5"],
  needs_note="operator answer F5 (wire as a projection of the frozen envelope)",
  risk="A client that read a dropped field breaks. Mitigation: only fields no LLM can use are dropped; the dropped list is documented in the server instructions. Rollback: revert.",
  docs="PROJECT-STATUS section 2 via EP-5."),

# ---------------- W4: rider and what it unblocks ----------------
t(id="RIDER-1", slug="foundation-signoff-rider", title="Raise the single foundation rider PR with only the adopted items",
  s=["review (D)","RV-5 F-5.6","RV-3 F-1.11","RV-6 F-A5","RV-1 F-1.10"], wave=4, area=["ops","eval","retrieval"], tier="Sonnet", size="M", signoff="y: this ticket IS the sign-off request; the operator merges (never an agent)",
  why="Several adopted changes can only land on protected paths (`contracts/`, `rag/config.py`, `config.example.yaml`, `rag/fakes/`, `fixtures/`, `.github/`), and every unrelated protected-path PR pays the same sign-off toll; batching them into one PR pays it once (`docs/AGENT-OPERATIONS-LESSONS.md` section 6.3). It is raised only after the wave-2 verdicts so only adopted items ride.",
  in_=["(1) `Config` fields (in `contracts/config.py`, loader/defaults in `rag/config.py`, `config.example.yaml`) for whichever of `drop_stub_chunks` (EV-21), the focus lever (RQ-3) and the query-path `gpu_lock_timeout` (OP-5) were ADOPTED; none if none were.","(2) `relevance_filter=\"embedding\"` fails validation until a gate exists (dead lever, RV-5 F-5.6).","(3) Only if EV-19's gate opened: the `rerank_score` metadata note in `contracts/retriever.py` and its DATA-CONTRACTS section M7 paragraph.","(4) `rag/fakes/fake_vector_store.py` imports the shared `sparse_tokens()` (RQ-5).","(5) Promote the three ground-truth sets to `fixtures/eval/` with one parametrised invariants test (unique ids, strata vocabulary, no gold on absent items, 6-word rule, excerpt verbatim in the live database with a skip when absent) and the SHA-256 in each set's metadata (RV-3 F-1.11), after the hash lock.","(6) `.github/`: a `ruff` step in CI and the nightly real-adapter workflow labelled manual-only (RV-6 F-A5).","Conditional item 7, present only if F7 = rewrite: DATA-CONTRACTS wording for `Block.section_path` (review S-24 sign-off need)."],
  out=["The `chunker_id` migration (explicitly not doing). Any logic change beyond the listed edits. Pushing to the default branch or merging (human only). Items whose verdict was REJECT or UNDERPOWERED: they drop out, the rider shrinks."],
  owns=["contracts/config.py","contracts/retriever.py","rag/config.py","config.example.yaml","rag/fakes/fake_vector_store.py","rag/fakes/test_fake_vector_store.py","fixtures/eval/","DATA-CONTRACTS.md",".github/workflows/ci.yml",".github/workflows/nightly-real-adapters.yml"],
  commits=["stub: PR description draft listing each item, its source verdict and the operator decision it needs; empty diff","items (4) and (5) (no verdict dependency)","items (1)-(3) for the adopted set only, each citing its verdict report","item (6) and conditional item 7","local enforcement transcript with the `foundation-change` label noted"],
  verify=["`conda run -n agent-rag-research python -m pytest -q -o addopts=\"--disable-socket -m 'not real_adapter'\"` (includes the new invariants test)","`EV=$(mktemp) && printf '{\"pull_request\":{\"number\":0,\"labels\":[\"foundation-change\"],\"base\":{\"sha\":\"%s\"},\"head\":{\"sha\":\"%s\"}}}' \"$(git merge-base origin/main HEAD)\" \"$(git rev-parse HEAD)\" > \"$EV\" && GITHUB_EVENT_NAME=pull_request GITHUB_EVENT_PATH=\"$EV\" conda run -n agent-rag-research python -m ci.run_enforcement`","Mutation proof for the invariants test: edit one question in a copy and watch it fail"],
  accept="One PR only; every protected-path edit is traceable to a listed item with an ADOPT verdict or an operator decision; the invariants test passes on the three promoted sets and fails when one question is altered; the PR carries the `foundation-change` label and waits for the operator's merge. Falsified if the PR touches any protected path not listed.",
  deps=["EV-11","EV-18","EV-19","EV-20","EV-21","RQ-3","RQ-5","OP-5","CQ-18"], ext=["F4","F7"], gates=["RQ-4","EP-5"],
  needs_note="operator sign-off and merge; push of the local commits so CI can judge them (F4)",
  risk="A broad rider is slow to review. Mitigation: items with no adopted verdict are omitted, so it can be small. A wrong Config default could change serving: all new fields default to current behaviour. Rollback: revert the merge (single PR).",
  docs="DATA-CONTRACTS section M7 paragraph for item (3) (in this PR); PROJECT-STATUS via EP-5."),

